abstract: >-
  A query factors through a sample profile on the image iff it is constant
  on the fibres. Two endpoint samples do not determine the midpoint. A
  decoder within epsilon bounds fibre collisions by 2 epsilon. Value equality
  under zero error requires the metric separation axiom. Lipschitz queries
  change at most by a constant times the input gap.
